Abstract

Version 5.1 incorporates the critical refinements proposed after Version 5.0. The central conditional Besov boundedness theorem (Theorem A) remains unchanged, with complete constant tracking. The passage to a dyadic Carleson regularity criterion is now strengthened by three concrete additions: (1) an explicit off-diagonal heat-kernel decay lemma that resolves the nonlocality objection to Lemma 6.1; (2) a Bony paraproduct decomposition of Conjecture 5.1 that isolates and controls the high-high frequency resonant term via sub-dyadic dissipation; and (3) an unconditional local Carleson bound for the axisymmetric no-swirl quantity Γ = ω^φ/r. The non-concentration hypothesis is maintained in maximal-function form with measure-theoretic exceptional sets. The program remains falsifiable, with clearly identified open ingredients. No unconditional regularity is claimed.

