7. Wavelet Program

The wavelet program remains as in Version 5.0, with the dyadic Carleson characterization (Hypothesis 9.1 of Version 5.0) now aligned with the Bony paraproduct decomposition in Section 5.2.

Hypothesis 7.1 (Dyadic Carleson wavelet characterization).
There exists a divergence-free orthonormal wavelet basis  \{\psi_\lambda\}_{\lambda\in\Lambda}  of  L^2_\sigma(\mathbb R^3)  such that

\|f\|_{\mathrm{BMO}^{-1}_{\rm dy}}
\sim
\sup_{Q\in\mathcal D}
\left(
\frac{1}{|Q|}
\sum_{\lambda:\,\mathrm{supp}\,\psi_\lambda\subset Q}
|c_\lambda|^2
\right)^{1/2},
\qquad c_\lambda=\langle f,\psi_\lambda\rangle.
\tag{7.1}

Under this hypothesis, the paraproduct decomposition becomes discrete and the resonant term control in Section 5.2.2 may be expressed in terms of wavelet coefficients.

